Description: Screens scientific manuscripts and data repositories and flags
    potential issues for improvement, to help researchers adopt best
    practices. It is an open source, modular tool that allows anyone to
    create automated checks. These checks are meant to assist, not replace,
    human expertise. It can check reporting guidelines (such as statements
    about conflicts of interest, funding, and ethics approval), statistical
    reporting (such as p values, power analyses, and effect sizes), and
    references (such as retracted or replicated studies). It also examines
    whether repositories, data, code, and codebooks are findable, accessible,
    interoperable, and reusable, and it can check whether the code in a
    repository reproduces its results.
